WEBVTT

00:04.830 --> 00:05.880
Good day.

00:05.880 --> 00:07.420
Oh, we're expecting you!

00:07.420 --> 00:10.090
The items you requested are finished!

00:10.090 --> 00:11.890
Hey, Rudy! Bring them here!

00:11.890 --> 00:13.130
Got it!

00:13.630 --> 00:15.010
Here they are.

00:16.350 --> 00:18.430
Wow, beautiful!

00:18.840 --> 00:20.770
Oh, this is awesome.

00:20.770 --> 00:22.730
There are these too!

00:23.560 --> 00:24.900
Amazing!

00:24.900 --> 00:26.690
These ones are so well-made too!

00:26.690 --> 00:28.360
Glad to hear.

00:28.360 --> 00:31.650
Evil Viper's skin
is such a wonderful material.

00:32.190 --> 00:34.610
It was a great experience for me too.

00:34.610 --> 00:36.820
Yes, this fits nicely.

00:36.820 --> 00:40.790
So, Young Man,
don't you bring the hawk?

00:40.790 --> 00:41.830
Huh?

00:41.830 --> 00:44.750
Well, I kind of do.

00:44.750 --> 00:47.880
Is it outside?
We don't mind so call it over.

00:48.920 --> 00:53.510
After all, that protection is for
when it lands on your arm, right?

00:53.510 --> 00:55.970
Let's try it out to test it.

00:55.970 --> 00:58.720
Oh, right. You're right...

00:58.720 --> 01:02.180
Actually, it's not a hawk
but a Summon...

01:02.180 --> 01:03.930
Huh? What's wrong?

01:04.430 --> 01:05.600
Fine then...

01:06.100 --> 01:07.350
Bolt!

01:10.500 --> 01:12.400
Where did it come from?!

01:12.400 --> 01:14.570
More importantly, isn't that...

01:14.570 --> 01:16.570
A Thunder Hawk?

01:16.570 --> 01:18.870
Oh, so you noticed?

01:23.700 --> 01:29.190
♪Leisurely, leisurely,
let's slowly familiarize ourselves♪

01:29.190 --> 01:34.690
(A Journey Through Another World:
Raising Kids While Adventuring)

01:35.340 --> 01:40.220
♪The adventure to a new world is beginning♪

01:40.470 --> 01:45.060
♪Into a journey where
we can find fun things♪

01:47.060 --> 01:51.940
♪There are many encounters,
it's so exciting♪

01:51.940 --> 01:58.110
♪If you're with your family,
the things you can do will multiply♪

01:58.110 --> 02:01.030
♪It's okay to worry,
but you must not be overprotective♪

02:01.030 --> 02:03.990
♪I want you to praise me when
I try something and succeed♪

02:03.990 --> 02:06.790
♪It will be a wonderful party
if we can do this and that♪

02:06.790 --> 02:11.670
♪Because we will be together forever♪

02:12.210 --> 02:15.460
♪Please pat my head♪

02:15.460 --> 02:17.970
♪With your hand that I truly love♪

02:17.970 --> 02:23.890
♪I will send you thank you from
the deepest part of my heart, okay?♪

02:23.890 --> 02:26.600
♪Please pat me more♪

02:26.600 --> 02:29.730
♪See me with those eyes
filled with kindness♪

02:29.730 --> 02:36.070
♪I want this smile to last,
forever and ever♪

02:36.070 --> 02:41.740
♪Leisurely, leisurely,
let's slowly walk on♪

02:42.240 --> 02:47.620
♪Leisurely, Yururing,
I am happy, Travel Days♪

02:50.770 --> 02:53.790
(Goodbye! See You Again!)

02:53.790 --> 02:54.770
(Goodbye! See You Again!)
Beautiful!

02:54.770 --> 02:55.460
Beautiful!

02:56.070 --> 02:58.010
Bolt, good boy!

03:00.880 --> 03:02.800
Good boy, good boy!

03:03.760 --> 03:04.890
I want to do it too!

03:04.890 --> 03:06.810
Bolt, good boy!

03:08.690 --> 03:11.770
Hey, can we hide Bolt already?

03:11.770 --> 03:13.270
The people are looking at you.

03:14.660 --> 03:15.730
Mr. Takumi.

03:16.190 --> 03:19.320
I have to ask, among the goods
found at the bandit hideout

03:19.320 --> 03:23.450
is there a painting
with a silver frame?

03:24.160 --> 03:25.910
Silver frame...

03:25.910 --> 03:28.620
Well, there are several paintings...

03:30.610 --> 03:31.630
Maybe this one?

03:32.080 --> 03:32.920
Wait!

03:35.250 --> 03:37.590
T-This is...

03:37.590 --> 03:39.550
...a little mature.

03:41.430 --> 03:42.510
Alan, Elena!

03:42.590 --> 03:44.800
Don't look at it too long!

03:44.800 --> 03:45.970
- Huh?
- Huh?

03:45.970 --> 03:52.690
If someone wants to buy it back,
would you allow them, Takumi?

03:52.690 --> 03:53.810
Sure.

03:53.810 --> 03:57.650
I originally planned to return them
once the owners are known.

03:57.650 --> 04:01.360
More importantly,
please store that away quickly...

04:01.360 --> 04:03.860
You're right. Joshua.

04:05.270 --> 04:06.450
It's fine now.

04:06.950 --> 04:08.830
Huh? It's gone.

04:08.830 --> 04:10.290
The painting is gone.

04:10.290 --> 04:14.540
Mr. Cedric asked me for it
so I gave it to him.

04:14.540 --> 04:16.040
Wait, Mr. Takumi!

04:16.040 --> 04:19.460
That makes it like
I'm the one who wanted it!

04:21.130 --> 04:24.130
Even you will get so flustered by it.

04:31.890 --> 04:34.560
After that, we went to the Azure Palace...

04:36.290 --> 04:37.790
The Mermaid Bracelet?

04:37.800 --> 04:41.990
Yes, I wonder if it is possible
to ask for more...

04:41.990 --> 04:44.950
But you already have them.

04:45.660 --> 04:46.910
Or perhaps...!

04:46.910 --> 04:49.410
Your current bracelet is broken?

04:49.410 --> 04:50.330
No, no.

04:50.330 --> 04:55.080
I have several Summons,
so I would like some for them.

04:55.080 --> 04:59.540
So that's why!
Then we'll prepare them right away.

05:00.490 --> 05:02.250
Sorry for the wait.

05:02.250 --> 05:05.510
If you need more,
just tell us anytime.

05:05.510 --> 05:07.430
Thank you very much.

05:07.430 --> 05:08.970
- Identical!
- Identical!

05:12.300 --> 05:16.650
Our next destination
is the unfinished Ripple labyrinth.

05:19.520 --> 05:21.610
We teleported to the 10th floor
with a device,

05:23.060 --> 05:25.350
then continued down
to the 11th floor.

05:26.010 --> 05:26.530
(Ripple Labyrinth, 11th floor)

05:26.530 --> 05:29.350
(Ripple Labyrinth, 11th floor)
The 11th floor was flooded.

05:29.350 --> 05:29.620
The 11th floor was flooded.

05:29.620 --> 05:30.910
- Water.
- Water.

05:30.910 --> 05:32.700
A part of them are flooded.

05:34.080 --> 05:37.160
We have the mermaid bracelet on,
so we won't get wet.

05:37.170 --> 05:40.670
Alan, Elena, tell me when you are tired.

05:40.670 --> 05:42.130
- Okay!
- Okay!

05:46.780 --> 05:47.800
- This way!
- This way!

05:48.220 --> 05:49.510
- Next is over here!
- Next is over here!

05:49.760 --> 05:52.410
- This way!
- This way!

05:52.410 --> 05:53.410
- That way!
- That way!

05:53.410 --> 05:54.470
- This way!
- This way!

05:55.640 --> 05:57.560
There is no monster...

05:57.560 --> 05:58.940
- There is none...
- There is none...

05:58.940 --> 06:01.400
Both of them look bored.

06:04.130 --> 06:05.740
Finally a monster?

06:13.620 --> 06:15.250
- Water Needle!
- Water Needle!

06:17.960 --> 06:19.580
- We beat it!
- We beat it!

06:19.580 --> 06:21.170
They're having so much fun.

06:21.170 --> 06:22.960
Great work!

06:22.960 --> 06:25.800
But was this way
really where you want to go?

06:25.800 --> 06:26.630
- Huh?
- Huh?

06:26.630 --> 06:30.340
Just now, you felt the monster's
presence and turned left, right?

06:34.310 --> 06:37.270
Oh, now you're laughing
to avoid the question.

06:37.640 --> 06:39.770
After that, we proceeded
while beating monsters

06:41.880 --> 06:44.800
and finding more hidden rooms.

06:46.920 --> 06:50.710
We found a dry place
and rested for the night.

06:52.340 --> 06:53.150
(Ripple Labyrinth, 17th floor)

06:53.150 --> 06:54.930
(Ripple Labyrinth, 17th floor)
And then the next day,

06:54.930 --> 06:56.580
we started from the 17th floor.

07:00.350 --> 07:02.500
It gets a little cold.

07:02.500 --> 07:05.090
Alan, Elena, put on these outerwear.

07:07.630 --> 07:09.470
- It's warm!
- It's warm!

07:12.720 --> 07:13.890
You're so cute.

07:13.890 --> 07:15.010
- A bear.
- A bear.

07:20.190 --> 07:23.310
A Water Ball, huh?
Well, I can do that as well.

07:25.360 --> 07:26.980
Water Ball!

07:33.390 --> 07:35.260
- Drop item!
- Drop item!

07:35.270 --> 07:37.790
Whoa, what a nice fur!

07:37.790 --> 07:40.770
Let's make a coat by using
this fur just for you.

07:40.770 --> 07:41.790
- Coat?
- Coat?

07:41.790 --> 07:43.920
They are clothes you put on
when it's cold.

07:43.920 --> 07:45.000
- What about these?
- What about these?

07:45.480 --> 07:48.310
Those won't be enough
if it gets even colder,

07:48.320 --> 07:49.960
so you need even warmer clothes!

07:51.970 --> 07:53.890
Alan wants Joule!

07:53.890 --> 07:55.510
Elena wants Feat!

07:56.480 --> 07:57.430
- These!
- These!

07:57.430 --> 08:00.890
Oh, you want the coat
to look like Joule and Feat?

08:00.890 --> 08:01.640
- Yes!
- Yes!

08:01.640 --> 08:05.190
Then, we will need a bit more fur.

08:05.190 --> 08:06.820
I wonder if the bear will come again.

08:06.820 --> 08:08.360
- There it is!
- There it is!

08:08.360 --> 08:10.070
A Bubble Archelon?

08:10.070 --> 08:11.990
It's not a bear...

08:12.530 --> 08:13.870
- What is it?
- What is it?

08:13.870 --> 08:14.990
It's a turtle.

08:17.120 --> 08:18.160
- Huh?
- Huh?

08:19.490 --> 08:21.910
Alan, Elena, do not touch that.

08:22.890 --> 08:26.460
The moment you touch it,
it will go boom and blast you away.

08:28.590 --> 08:29.750
- Okay!
- Okay!

08:30.420 --> 08:34.090
Bubble Archelon tends to hinder
their enemies with these bubbles

08:34.090 --> 08:36.300
and then run away.

08:37.900 --> 08:39.480
How do we defeat it?

08:40.110 --> 08:42.430
I know! This trick might work.

08:43.850 --> 08:44.980
Inventory!

08:48.570 --> 08:49.690
By using inventory,

08:49.690 --> 08:52.330
we can safely collect them
without breaking them.

08:52.330 --> 08:53.530
- Safely!
- Safely!

08:54.490 --> 08:55.570
Whoopsie!

08:55.570 --> 08:56.990
You can't run away!

08:56.990 --> 08:58.450
Water Pillar!

09:01.580 --> 09:02.950
Now, hit it!

09:04.750 --> 09:05.370
Nice!

09:05.370 --> 09:07.630
- We beat it!
- We took this!

09:08.900 --> 09:11.960
- Beary bear! Turtly turtle!

09:11.960 --> 09:13.400
- After that, we continued...
- Beary bear! Turtly turtle!

09:13.400 --> 09:14.670
- After that, we continued...

09:14.670 --> 09:15.800
That's dangerous!

09:15.800 --> 09:18.090
- We stepped on it.
- We stepped on it.

09:18.090 --> 09:20.310
Laughing like that is cute
so I'll forgive you.

09:20.970 --> 09:22.270
We continued smoothly.

09:24.730 --> 09:27.650
We had meals and slept.

09:30.360 --> 09:32.150
The water level increased,

09:32.150 --> 09:35.360
so we had Joule and the Summons
helped us to continue smoothly.

09:38.280 --> 09:40.780
Black Alligator?

09:40.780 --> 09:43.240
Big Bro, leave this to me!

09:49.730 --> 09:52.300
Having fire elemental,
Vector hates getting wet

09:52.300 --> 09:53.780
- so the additional Mermaid bracelets
work like a charm.

09:53.780 --> 09:55.420
- Vector, you're amazing!
- so the additional Mermaid bracelets
work like a charm.

09:55.420 --> 09:55.760
- so the additional Mermaid bracelets
work like a charm.

09:57.200 --> 09:59.970
- Well then, let's go further!
- Wait! That way is...

10:02.820 --> 10:05.890
Big Brother, I can't move...

10:06.430 --> 10:09.270
We finally arrived at the last floor
where the last boss was.

10:10.030 --> 10:11.440
- Is the boss here?
- Is the boss here?

10:11.440 --> 10:13.320
Maybe. Want to go look?

10:13.320 --> 10:14.110
- Let's go!
- Let's go!

10:31.710 --> 10:33.130
- The sea?
- The sea?

10:33.130 --> 10:35.090
There is a seashore in this room...

10:37.590 --> 10:39.840
Joule, take care of Alan and Elena!

10:39.840 --> 10:41.340
Yes, leave it to me!

10:43.190 --> 10:44.010
Is that...?

10:44.910 --> 10:45.970
Appraise!

10:46.070 --> 10:46.580
(Little Kraken)

10:46.720 --> 10:48.940
Wait, Little Kraken?

10:49.690 --> 10:52.150
That's not little at all.

10:53.860 --> 10:55.020
Wind Cutter!

10:59.700 --> 11:01.490
Instant regeneration?

11:02.490 --> 11:06.160
Water Jet!

11:09.540 --> 11:11.000
It keeps regenerating.

11:11.000 --> 11:12.580
There is no end to this.

11:12.590 --> 11:16.090
Big Brother, maybe it is better for us
to attack at the same time

11:16.090 --> 11:18.050
and kill it in one swoop.

11:18.050 --> 11:20.710
That sounds fun, I agree!

11:20.710 --> 11:21.510
Yes, yes!

11:21.510 --> 11:23.470
- Me too!
- You're right.

11:23.970 --> 11:25.930
We don't know how far
it could regenerate.

11:25.930 --> 11:27.640
That's a better way.

11:27.640 --> 11:28.980
I will help too!

11:31.190 --> 11:32.850
Then, let's do this.

11:32.860 --> 11:34.810
Wind Cutter!

11:34.810 --> 11:36.770
- Water Ball!
- Water Ball!

11:36.780 --> 11:38.110
Water Jet!

11:38.110 --> 11:39.650
Wind Cutter!

11:39.650 --> 11:40.900
Fire Ball!

11:40.910 --> 11:42.280
Thunder Bolt!

11:47.930 --> 11:49.750
It got blown to bits.

11:49.750 --> 11:52.710
I think the attack was too powerful.

11:54.250 --> 11:55.710
The sea is gone!

11:56.210 --> 11:57.290
You're right.

11:57.300 --> 11:58.670
A door!

12:01.280 --> 12:02.620
- Treasure chest!
- Treasure chest!

12:05.400 --> 12:06.510
- What is that?
- What is that?

12:06.510 --> 12:07.560
A sword.

12:07.560 --> 12:09.020
So huge!

12:09.020 --> 12:12.190
It appears to be a sword
enchanted with fire magic.

12:12.810 --> 12:15.820
I don't know if I can use it,
but let's take it.

12:15.820 --> 12:16.940
Inventory.

12:19.690 --> 12:23.490
Well, we're done with the boss,
now let's go back to the city.

12:23.490 --> 12:24.570
Yeah!

12:25.420 --> 12:27.950
Once we get out,
there may be other people

12:27.950 --> 12:29.990
so Joule and the others must hide.

12:29.990 --> 12:31.330
Is that so...

12:31.330 --> 12:33.450
Big Bro, call me soon, okay?

12:33.460 --> 12:36.040
- Big Brother, me too.
- Me too!

12:36.040 --> 12:38.290
Alan, Elena, see you again.

12:38.290 --> 12:39.840
- Bye-bye!
- Bye-bye!

12:39.840 --> 12:44.260
And so, we returned to Bailey
after several days of being away.

12:44.760 --> 12:46.470
Welcome back, Mr. Takumi.

12:46.470 --> 12:48.720
Yes, we're finally back.

12:48.720 --> 12:49.930
- We're back.
- We're back.

12:49.930 --> 12:51.830
How was the labyrinth?

12:51.830 --> 12:53.270
We want to hear the stories!

12:53.270 --> 12:56.400
Alan, Elena, did you defeat monsters?

12:56.400 --> 12:57.610
- We did!
- We did!

12:57.610 --> 12:59.270
What did you beat?

12:59.270 --> 13:00.670
Were they strong?

13:00.670 --> 13:03.670
Let's hear the story later, okay?

13:04.230 --> 13:08.630
Actually, there are others
who waited for Mr. Takumi's return.

13:09.970 --> 13:11.360
Yo, Takumi!

13:11.360 --> 13:13.290
It's been a while, Mr. Takumi.

13:13.540 --> 13:16.800
What?! Sir Vault! Mr. Issac!

13:18.720 --> 13:20.960
Kiddos, have you been doing well?

13:20.960 --> 13:22.300
- We're fine!
- We're fine!

13:22.300 --> 13:26.840
More importantly,
why are both of you here?

13:26.840 --> 13:29.260
- We come to fetch you, Takumi.
- What?

13:29.260 --> 13:32.270
Captain, stop skipping explanations.

13:32.270 --> 13:35.980
Um... Mr. Issac, what's going on...

13:35.980 --> 13:40.780
Sorry, I just suddenly started
calling you by name.

13:40.790 --> 13:41.940
It's okay.

13:42.480 --> 13:45.280
It can be both my brother and me
if you call me Risner.

13:45.280 --> 13:46.650
Thank you very much.

13:46.650 --> 13:49.200
And so, what do you mean by fetch?

13:49.200 --> 13:54.160
So recently we went to
the royal capital for a mission.

13:54.160 --> 13:55.750
Oh, you did?

13:55.750 --> 13:59.790
So, there's this guy who found
a new labyrinth in Bailey.

13:59.790 --> 14:01.130
Eh?

14:01.130 --> 14:03.710
His Majesty wants to meet him.

14:03.710 --> 14:06.800
But that man dislikes being
the center of attention...

14:07.720 --> 14:12.460
His Majesty said he wanted to avoid
making the man uncomfortable.

14:12.460 --> 14:14.680
Excuse me, that's me...

14:14.680 --> 14:19.650
And so, we, who are acquainted
with you, got the mission.

14:19.650 --> 14:21.940
He told us to bring you
to the royal capital.

14:21.940 --> 14:24.150
- That's the story!
- Captain.

14:24.150 --> 14:24.640
- His Majesty means the King, right?

14:24.640 --> 14:26.670
- I was the one who explained it all.
- His Majesty means the King, right?

14:26.670 --> 14:28.760
- Don't fuss about the details.
- You mean the King is asking for us?

14:28.760 --> 14:29.360
- You mean the King is asking for us?

14:30.180 --> 14:33.580
Mr. Takumi, would you go
to the royal capital with us?

14:36.700 --> 14:38.710
The King of the Kingdom of Guadia...

14:38.710 --> 14:41.250
Meeting him won't be bad.

14:41.250 --> 14:47.010
Alan, Elena, do you mind if we leave
for another city for a while?

14:47.010 --> 14:48.600
You will go too?

14:48.600 --> 14:49.470
Of course.

14:49.470 --> 14:51.110
Then Alan will go!

14:51.120 --> 14:52.430
Elena too!

14:52.800 --> 14:54.930
These kids said okay, so...

14:54.930 --> 14:57.600
Right! It's better to do it soon.

14:57.600 --> 15:00.140
It's not good to make the King wait.

15:00.140 --> 15:02.520
I understand that you're still tired,

15:02.520 --> 15:05.980
but if possible, we want to leave
tomorrow morning.

15:05.980 --> 15:07.530
Tomorrow morning?

15:10.320 --> 15:12.570
Theodore, Lantis...

15:12.570 --> 15:14.160
I see...

15:14.160 --> 15:19.790
If we leave this city tomorrow,
that'll mean saying goodbye to them too.

15:20.330 --> 15:23.580
Do Alan and Elena understand that?

15:25.780 --> 15:27.050
Alan, Elena.

15:27.050 --> 15:28.300
- What is it?
- What is it?

15:29.100 --> 15:30.220
You see...

15:33.090 --> 15:35.890
Nah, maybe not right now.
Rather than that...

15:35.890 --> 15:39.230
I remember! We found something
interesting in the labyrinth,

15:39.230 --> 15:40.850
want to play with it?

15:40.850 --> 15:44.560
Let's make the kids
a lot of happy memories.

15:44.560 --> 15:46.820
Wow, what are these?

15:46.820 --> 15:47.780
So soft!

15:47.780 --> 15:51.470
Theodore, try hitting it
with your hand and make it fly.

15:51.470 --> 15:52.740
A-All right!

15:52.740 --> 15:53.700
Like this?

15:54.660 --> 15:57.370
Alan! Try hitting it to Latis's side.

15:57.370 --> 15:58.740
Do it gently.

15:58.740 --> 15:59.580
Okay!

16:00.080 --> 16:01.790
- Next, to Elena.
- There!

16:03.120 --> 16:04.960
Elena, pass it to Theodore.

16:06.130 --> 16:08.550
You're doing great! Keep it up!

16:08.550 --> 16:09.630
Elena!

16:19.680 --> 16:22.060
The kids are getting closer, right?

16:22.060 --> 16:25.230
Yes. Alan and Elena got close already.

16:25.230 --> 16:29.940
It's even harder to tell them
we'll leave Theodore and the others.

16:29.940 --> 16:32.700
By the way, what is that ball?

16:32.700 --> 16:34.910
That's the bubble produced
by Bubble Archelon.

16:34.910 --> 16:35.780
What?

16:35.780 --> 16:38.950
The one that'll burst if you touch it?
Why isn't it breaking?

16:39.580 --> 16:42.870
It doesn't burst anymore
after I put it into my inventory.

16:42.870 --> 16:45.420
So I thought we could play with it.

16:46.330 --> 16:47.790
- Let's play together!
- Let's play together!

16:47.790 --> 16:49.810
Would you play with us, Uncles?

16:49.810 --> 16:51.760
Sir Vault, let's have a match!

16:51.760 --> 16:54.720
All right! You kiddos!
I'll be your enemy!

16:54.970 --> 16:56.580
Here we go!

16:56.580 --> 16:58.390
- Come at me!
- There!

16:58.390 --> 17:00.260
- Here!
- That's so high!

17:00.260 --> 17:02.850
After that, we ate a lively meal

17:02.850 --> 17:06.520
and the adults went to have
some drinks for our last night.

17:07.100 --> 17:08.520
In the end,

17:08.520 --> 17:12.110
I wasn't able to tell the two they'd say
goodbye to Theodore and the others.

17:13.110 --> 17:15.550
I should've said that
in the beginning.

17:17.940 --> 17:18.950
Excuse me.

17:20.210 --> 17:21.870
Are the kids already asleep?

17:21.870 --> 17:24.870
Yes. Right after they got into bed.

17:24.870 --> 17:26.420
I see.

17:28.750 --> 17:30.590
- Here.
- Ah, thank you.

17:30.590 --> 17:33.920
I thought they wouldn't let you go.

17:34.420 --> 17:37.470
They are completely glued
to you after all.

17:37.470 --> 17:40.970
Due to the place where they grew up,
you can't blame them.

17:40.970 --> 17:42.350
What do you mean?

17:44.350 --> 17:48.400
It appears Alan and Elena
were alone in a horrid place.

17:49.110 --> 17:51.230
That's why they're glued to you.

17:51.230 --> 17:55.700
But like this, they could separate
from him for a bit.

17:55.700 --> 17:57.070
It's really good.

17:57.720 --> 17:58.860
That's true.

17:59.870 --> 18:04.250
In the beginning, they were afraid
of meeting strangers.

18:04.590 --> 18:07.370
Then they started to warm up
to the people in the city...

18:07.370 --> 18:10.000
And they make friends
with other children.

18:12.040 --> 18:15.670
It's slowly, but they are growing.

18:15.670 --> 18:19.890
So that means you are not
blood-related, then?

18:19.890 --> 18:23.350
You can say being blood-related
or not doesn't matter,

18:23.350 --> 18:25.770
with how much of a family they are!

18:31.270 --> 18:39.820
Once I thought what I did make
a difference, I felt like crying.

18:41.160 --> 18:43.700
Sir Vault, thank you.

18:44.540 --> 18:46.500
What, are you bawling?

18:47.000 --> 18:48.960
I-I am not.

18:48.960 --> 18:51.380
Come on, let's drink the night away!

18:51.380 --> 18:52.460
Yes, Sir.

19:01.010 --> 19:03.340
And so, the morning of departure came.

19:04.850 --> 19:06.930
Alan doesn't want to go!

19:06.930 --> 19:08.560
Elena too!

19:10.060 --> 19:12.560
That's because Takumi didn't tell them.

19:12.560 --> 19:16.780
But I think the result
will be the same even if he did.

19:17.610 --> 19:19.490
- Your tea, Sir.
- Thank you.

19:19.950 --> 19:21.620
Listen up, you two.

19:21.620 --> 19:26.250
This does not mean you will never
meet Theodore and Latis again.

19:27.350 --> 19:28.870
Alan wants to stay here!

19:28.870 --> 19:30.870
Elena wants to play more!

19:30.870 --> 19:32.790
- Alan...
- Elena...

19:33.790 --> 19:36.250
Are they getting away from Takumi?!

19:37.000 --> 19:39.720
This means the royal capital trip
is canceled, right?

19:43.210 --> 19:44.920
There's nothing we can do.

19:44.920 --> 19:46.890
Let's cancel the trip
to the royal capital.

19:46.890 --> 19:49.820
Yeah, make up some
excuses to the King.

19:49.820 --> 19:52.690
Don't put it all on me,
try doing it yourself sometimes.

19:52.690 --> 19:55.900
Alan, Elena, do you want to wait here?

19:56.400 --> 19:58.020
What?!

19:58.610 --> 20:00.990
Mr. Cedric, pardon me for this,

20:00.990 --> 20:03.950
but could you take care
of them until I return?

20:03.950 --> 20:06.490
We don't mind, but...

20:07.780 --> 20:11.290
But will Alan and Elena
be fine with that?

20:13.840 --> 20:15.840
You're okay with that, Takumi?

20:16.380 --> 20:17.090
Yeah.

20:17.960 --> 20:21.050
I can't call it a rebellious phase yet.

20:21.050 --> 20:23.180
But now for Alan and Elena,

20:23.180 --> 20:27.390
friends their age must be
more important than me.

20:28.750 --> 20:30.460
Now, I will be leaving.

20:30.460 --> 20:32.670
Alan and Elena, be good kids, okay?

20:35.900 --> 20:38.620
Takumi! Are you sure about this?!

20:38.630 --> 20:40.630
Don't ask me again and again.

20:40.630 --> 20:41.440
Well...

20:41.440 --> 20:43.900
That's because your shadows are bubbling.

20:47.620 --> 20:50.200
- Big Bro!
- Big Bro!

20:54.350 --> 20:55.970
Alan! Elena!

20:59.930 --> 21:02.250
- Alan! Elena!
- Big Bro!

21:03.970 --> 21:06.930
Alan! Elena!

21:06.930 --> 21:09.390
I don't want us to get separated!

21:09.390 --> 21:11.850
We will always be together!

21:11.850 --> 21:14.060
- I think so too!
- Me too!

21:14.600 --> 21:16.190
What are those?

21:16.190 --> 21:19.020
Perhaps it's Mr. Takumi's Summons...

21:23.240 --> 21:26.200
He keeps surprising us all the time.

21:28.030 --> 21:29.870
Alan, Elena...

21:29.870 --> 21:32.080
- We'll go together with you!
- We'll go together with you!

21:35.650 --> 21:39.570
Then you must properly say goodbye
to Theodore and Latis.

21:44.750 --> 21:48.880
Be well, Alan, Elena.
We will send you letters.

21:48.880 --> 21:52.010
Even if we're apart,
we will always be friends!

21:52.770 --> 21:54.430
So let's play together again later!

21:59.650 --> 22:00.650
- Yeah!
- Yeah!

22:05.340 --> 22:06.900
Well then, we'll be leaving!

22:06.900 --> 22:08.200
Bye bye!

22:08.950 --> 22:10.450
Goodbye!

22:10.450 --> 22:11.490
Be careful!

22:14.950 --> 22:17.710
- See you!
- Goodbye!

22:20.850 --> 22:22.010
And so...

22:22.580 --> 22:25.170
...our journey to
the royal capital has started.

22:31.050 --> 22:35.520
♪Forever, all the time♪

22:35.520 --> 22:38.440
♪I just can't keep crying♪

22:38.440 --> 22:39.650
♪Ah! Ah!♪

22:39.650 --> 22:43.110
♪In happy moments and sad moments♪

22:43.110 --> 22:45.730
♪If I am with you♪

22:47.990 --> 22:50.030
♪Such a good weather♪

22:50.030 --> 22:53.620
♪Today, let's go slowly♪

22:53.620 --> 22:55.870
♪While taking detours♪

22:55.870 --> 23:00.420
♪The clear sky,
the wind caressing my cheeks♪

23:00.420 --> 23:03.670
♪And your gentle gaze♪

23:03.670 --> 23:06.920
♪Beyond an unknown road♪

23:06.920 --> 23:08.970
♪The wind blows past♪

23:08.970 --> 23:11.970
♪The curtain of light sways♪

23:12.720 --> 23:16.350
♪Maybe we should try going
I just feel like it♪

23:16.350 --> 23:22.860
♪No matter what happens
we can laugh anyway♪

23:25.070 --> 23:29.070
♪Forever, all the time♪

23:29.320 --> 23:32.070
♪I just can't keep crying♪

23:32.070 --> 23:33.320
♪Ah! Ah!♪

23:33.320 --> 23:36.830
♪In happy moments and sad moments♪

23:36.830 --> 23:40.000
♪If I am with you♪

23:41.170 --> 23:45.960
♪I am sure I'll be content♪
